        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "I thought the costume test and the costume portion of the final exam were much harder than they needed to be. A lot of the information was not covered in the lectures and was far too in-depth for a survey course.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 2
            },
            {
                "comment": "A fairly easy class, maybe a little challenging for non-theatre students who aren't familiar with the topics. Jim has a very blunt sense of humor, so if you get offended easily, avoid this class. Stay on his good side!",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "Although Theatre 160 is a collaboratively taught class by 4 instructors, Jim definitely takes the lead. It's clear that he enjoys teaching his section. He responds to emails promptly and has a very clear syllabus. Show up to the classes and you'll be just fine!",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Jim is very organized and responsive.  His syllabuses are very helpful and he always lets you know what is going on.  He grades things right away and is fair--gives reasons for lower grades.  He has a fun sense of humor to go with all the great information that he also has to offer.  Without one of his classes, your theatre experience isn't comlete",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            }
